# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
#
# `key.properties` names the release keystore and holds its passwords, so it is
# ignored file-first: releasing it once is enough to let anyone publish an
# update that Android will happily install over the real app. The patterns below
# are unanchored on purpose — a keystore dropped in `android/`, in `app/`, or in
# a `keys/` subdirectory during a hurried release is still ignored, which a
# top-level `/upload.jks` rule would miss.
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/*.p12
